# Real-Time Bus Tracking System

**Author:** Sauryakul Raj

## Overview

The **Real-Time Bus Tracking System** is a full-stack web application that allows users to monitor the live location of a bus on an interactive map.
The system simulates real-time bus movement along a road route and displays key travel information such as **distance remaining, estimated time of arrival (ETA), and speed**.

The project demonstrates how modern transportation tracking systems work using mapping services and real-time data updates.

---

## Features

* 🗺 **Interactive Map** using OpenStreetMap
* 🛣 **Road Route Visualization** between Delhi and Chandigarh
* 🚌 **Real-Time Bus Movement Simulation**
* 📍 **Bus Stop Markers**
* ⏱ **Estimated Time of Arrival (ETA)** calculation
* 📏 **Distance Remaining** display
* 🚍 **Speed Simulation**
* 🔁 **Automatic Reverse Movement** (bus travels back from destination)

---

## Technologies Used

### Frontend

* React.js
* Leaflet
* React Leaflet

### Backend

* FastAPI (Python)

### APIs

* OpenRouteService (route generation)
* OpenStreetMap (map tiles)

---

## System Architecture

```
Frontend (React + Leaflet)
        ↓
Backend API (FastAPI)
        ↓
OpenRouteService API
        ↓
Map Rendering (OpenStreetMap)
```

The frontend fetches route data and updates the bus position periodically to simulate real-time tracking.

